n below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[N\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=12{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{N}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c56b3e9-cf23-5e1e-8c7d-c474059c9a9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef815bd-f246-5489-a173-af59955aa440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388162} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b90574-37d3-5939-9d6d-f41a132e44c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{7} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388163} {:answer/id #uuid "e0797fd8-3780-510c-a616-159309484a73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388164} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6a68cc-a941-50cf-87a0-dbba7667c8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388165} {:answer/id #uuid "2f63056e-6d68-5d2d-a877-8755ac4c2845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e