$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{W}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd12bc7b-1b5d-5af2-bcef-c9d0fda7d8fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171d85cf-363f-5e91-8844-7377fbfe4868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550417} {:answer/id #uuid "abc41fe2-4fc6-5168-adaa-26ac614241df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550831} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d97c63-845a-5df4-bd21-ef85ce115fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550877} {:answer/id #uuid "d05c1129-f39e-5113-b571-d89546b3420c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550927} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b02096-c5f8-533f-a7c6-397872aa44c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "171d85cf-363f-5e91-8844-7377fbfe4868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550417} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa55760-fe42-5b20-a3f8-0684f066d9d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5238d337-5418-5670-995a-6cacdf9c34e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-130816" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{1}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{1}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{1}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd12bc7b-1b5d-5af2-bcef-c9d0fda7d8fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359a8301-f2b5-525c-9c59-3eca56ed7220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550498} {:answer/id #uuid "954ac438-6aab-5e66-944b-f44c338618fb" :answer/type {