s the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{1}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265982 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd12bc7b-1b5d-5af2-bcef-c9d0fda7d8fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0449b553-1b65-5cac-8598-b0d8a270a950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263039} {:answer/id #uuid "08cf208e-4a67-56fb-af8e-a3fd93304b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263084} {:answer/id #uuid "79e21f99-e8cc-51c3-a318-a7ddd869b864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264057} {:answer/id #uuid "7e60b2a6-6056-5ea2-8a17-c6be4b8de34e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}19 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264091} {:answer/id #uuid "9e4de5ce-9af6-520d-b7aa-ae9f2db45567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 & -7 \\\\ 8 & -1